.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt OSSL_PARAM_DUP 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm OSSL_PARAM_dup ,
.Nm OSSL_PARAM_merge ,
.Nm OSSL_PARAM_free
.Nd OSSL_PARAM array copy functions
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/params.h
.Ft OSSL_PARAM *
.Fo OSSL_PARAM_dup
.Fa "const OSSL_PARAM *params"
.Fc
.Ft OSSL_PARAM *
.Fo OSSL_PARAM_merge
.Fa "const OSSL_PARAM *params"
.Fa "const OSSL_PARAM *params1"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo OSSL_PARAM_free
.Fa "OSSL_PARAM *params"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Algorithm parameters can be exported/imported from/to providers using
arrays of
.Xr OSSL_PARAM 3 .
The following utility functions allow the parameters to be duplicated
and merged with other
.Xr OSSL_PARAM 3
to assist in this process.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_PARAM_dup
duplicates the parameter array
.Fa params .
This function does a deep copy of the data.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_PARAM_merge
merges the parameter arrays
.Fa params
and
.Fa params1
into a new parameter array.
If
.Fa params
and
.Fa params1
contain values with the same 'key' then the value from
.Fa params1
will replace the
.Em param
value.
This function does a shallow copy of the parameters.
Either
.Fa params
or
.Fa params1
may be NULL. The behaviour of the merge is unpredictable if
.Fa params
and
.Fa params1
contain the same key, and there are multiple entries within either array
that have the same key.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_PARAM_free
frees the parameter array
.Fa params
that was created using
.Fn OSSL_PARAM_dup ,
.Fn OSSL_PARAM_merge
or
.Xr OSSL_PARAM_BLD_to_param 3 .
If the argument to
.Fn OSSL_PARAM_free
is NULL, nothing is done.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The functions
.Fn OSSL_PARAM_dup
and
.Fn OSSL_PARAM_merge
return a newly allocated
.Xr OSSL_PARAM 3
array, or NULL if there was an error.
If both parameters are NULL
.br
then NULL is returned.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr OSSL_PARAM 3 ,
.Xr OSSL_PARAM_BLD 3
.Sh HISTORY
The functions were added in OpenSSL 3.0.
